{"title":"Manipal (MET)","category":"Engineering","bank":"manipal_met","subject":"Chemistry","chapter":"Polymers","count":10,"questions":[{"id":53034,"subject":"Chemistry","chapter":"Polymers","exam":"Engineering","examName":"Manipal (MET)","q":"PDI for natural polymers is generally close to","options":["zero","1","10","100"],"answer":1,"solution":"PDI abbreviates as polydispersity index of polymer.\n$\\mathrm{PDI}=\\frac{\\bar{M}_w}{M_n}$\nFor natural polymers, $\\mathrm{PDI}=1$\nand for synthetic polymers, PDI $>1$","difficulty":"Medium","source":"Manipal (MET) 2012","_marksId":"67921db41d5b5072da5e9d3c"},{"id":53035,"subject":"Chemistry","chapter":"Polymers","exam":"Engineering","examName":"Manipal (MET)","q":"Which one is chain growth polymer?","options":["Teflon","Nylon-6","Nylon-66","Bakelite"],"answer":0,"solution":"$Chain growth polymers are formed by the chain growth polymerisation or chain polymerisation. This polymerisation process involves in a series of reaction each of which consumes a relative particles and produces another similar particle resulting a chain reaction. Teflon is a chain growth polymer. It is the polymer of tetraflouro ethylene.\n\\left.\\underset{\\text{ Tetrofluoro ethylene }}{n\\left(\\mathrm{CF}_2\\right.}=\\mathrm{CF}_2\\right) \\xrightarrow[\\text{ Pressure }]{\\text{ High }}-\\left(\\mathrm{CF}_2 \\underset{\\text{ Teflon }}{\\left.-\\mathrm{CF}_2\\right)_n}\\right.$","difficulty":"Medium","source":"Manipal (MET) 2015","_marksId":"67921dff1d5b5072da5e9f87"},{"id":53036,"subject":"Chemistry","chapter":"Polymers","exam":"Engineering","examName":"Manipal (MET)","q":"Natural rubber is a polymer of monomer isoprene. During polymerisaton","options":["1, 4 addition takes place","1,2 addition takes place","1, 3 addition takes place","both double bonds are converted into single bond"],"answer":0,"solution":"Natural rubber is a linear polymers of isoprene and is also called as cis-1, 4-polyisoprene.\nIt is a linear 1, 4-polymer of isoprene